  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nSaturday Night/Sunday Morning: Surface high pressure does look\nto slide over the area and REFS guidance depicts a higher\nprobability for less clouds, patchy fog northwest of \nSpringfield and overall higher frost/freeze potential with lows \nin the 30s (20s east of Springfield). If we do not have a \nsufficiently cold night tonight then additional frost/freeze \nheadlines would be needed for Saturday night given a more likely\ncolder night. After a cold start Sunday morning, clear skies on\nSunday should allow for temps to warmer closer to average in \nthe 60s.\n\nWarmer and Dry Next Week: Ensemble Cluster Analysis continues to\nsuggest a west/northwest flow pattern across our area for early\nand mid week with disturbances remaining either north or south \nof the area. Precip chances remain less than 10 percent this \nweek. NBM interquartile spreads are generally less than 5 \ndegrees which suggest high confidence of above average highs \nwith temps approaching 70 Monday through Wednesday. Uncertainty \nin the pattern does appear Thursday and Friday as energy slides \ndown from the north into the area and may bring another shot of \ncooler air.",
